Subject: [PATCH 1/4] chore: SEO/legal/blog/CI polish pass, on top of the LMS
 content delivery work
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ported from a parallel branch built against Bengo-Hub/main; applied cleanly
here since none of the files this touches overlap with the course-content-
delivery commit.

- Remove stray committed .patch file (0001-feat-digitika-...patch) — looks
  like an artifact from applying a patch that got added with a stray
  `git add -A` rather than actually run through `git am`.
- sitemap.xml + robots.txt (dynamic — live courses + published blog posts)
- .env.local.example, built from every process.env.* reference actually
  used in the code
- public/.well-known/security.txt (RFC 9116) + /security disclosure page
- Cookie consent banner (accept/decline, first-party cookie, reopenable via
  footer 'Cookie settings' link) + privacy policy: added a Kenya Data
  Protection Act 2019 section (was GDPR-only) and a cookies section
- JSON-LD structured data: Organization (site-wide), Course (course detail
  pages), BlogPosting (blog post pages) — src/lib/json-ld.tsx
- Blog: wired /blog and new /blog/[slug] to the existing BlogPost model +
  seed data instead of a hardcoded 6-post array. Renders with
  react-markdown+remark-gfm (already a dependency, previously unused).
  Added 'blog' to the RBAC module catalog + admin CRUD
  (GET/POST /api/admin/blog, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/admin/blog/[id]).
- CI: added a blocking quality-gate job (lint + prisma generate + typecheck)
  that sync-secrets/deploy now depend on — previously nothing checked the
  actual code before it shipped.

Found but NOT fixed here (flagging, not fixing without confirming first):
admin-nav.ts (from the content-delivery commit) links to /admin/content and
/admin/certificates, but neither page exists yet — both are live 404s in
the admin panel right now. The API routes are all there
(admin/courses/[id]/modules, admin/modules/[id]/lessons,
admin/lessons/[id], admin/lessons/[id]/quiz) and the 'content'/'certificates'
permission modules are already in the RBAC catalog — just the two admin
pages themselves are missing.
